---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="About"
  description="Tanay Kashyap — thinking about why systems are designed the way they are, and what a more deliberate version might look like."
  currentPath="/about">
  <section class="about-page">
    <h1>About Baniloo</h1>

    <div class="about-content">
      <p>
        I've always been more interested in the question underneath the question — not what to build, but why things are designed the way they are, and whether that's the right design or just the one nobody thought to question.
      </p>

      <p>
        Most systems carry assumptions that were never made explicit. I think it's worth making them explicit — even when the answer turns out to be "this is more complicated than it seems."
      </p>

      <p>
        Baniloo is where that thinking lives. I'm not a builder yet. I'm a thinker working toward building, and I try to hold that honestly.
      </p>

      <p>
        The name comes from my parents' names — Bani and Niloo, a nickname for Mrityunjay. It felt right to build something under a name that meant something before this did.
      </p>

      <p>
        If something here starts a conversation worth having, I'm reachable at <a href="mailto:tanaykashyap.dev@gmail.com">tanaykashyap.dev@gmail.com</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>

<style>
  .about-page h1 {
    font-family: 'Fraunces', serif;
    font-size: 44px;
    font-weight: 600;
    line-height: 1.1;
    letter-spacing: -0.02em;
    color: var(--text);
    margin-bottom: 48px;
  }

  .about-content {
    max-width: 720px;
  }

  .about-content p {
    font-size: 17px;
    line-height: 1.8;
    color: var(--text);
    margin-bottom: 1.6em;
  }

  .about-content p:last-child {
    margin-bottom: 0;
  }

  .about-content a {
    color: var(--accent);
    text-decoration: none;
    transition: opacity 150ms ease;
  }

  .about-content a:hover {
    opacity: 0.8;
  }

  @media (max-width: 600px) {
    .about-page h1 {
      font-size: 32px;
    }
  }
</style>